# <type>(<scope>): <subject in the imperative, no trailing period>
#
# Then a blank line, then the body. Explain WHY, not what the diff
# already shows. Wrap every body line at 120 characters — never write the
# body as one long -m string, it will be rejected.
#
# ── Limits (enforced by .husky/commit-msg and by CI) ──────────────
#   header (the first line)   ≤ 100 characters
#   each body line            ≤ 120 characters
#   subject                   imperative, lower-case, NO trailing period
#   blank line                required between subject and body
#
# ── type ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   feat  fix  refactor  perf  test  docs  chore  ci  build  style  revert
#
# ── scope — CLOSED list. Anything else is rejected. ───────────────
#   Domain (server/domains/*):
#     costing  library  sales  planning
#     quality  security  basis  mes
#   Platform (cross-cutting):
#     platform  platform/auth  platform/audit  platform/cache
#     platform/sync  platform/i18n  platform/ui-kit  platform/http
#     platform/storage  platform/observability
#   App shells:
#     apps  apps/server  apps/client  apps/desktop
#   Tooling:
#     ci  deps  docs  tests
#     release
#
#   The scope follows the DOMAIN, not the folder name. There is no
#   pricing / server / client / desktop / help / scripts / ops scope —
#   use costing, apps/server, apps/client, apps/desktop, docs, tests.
#   The scope may be omitted (a warning, not an error).
#
# ── Trailers ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   Writing "Closes MES-3-FIX-N" mid-prose is fine — that rule is off
#   on purpose. Real trailers (Co-Authored-By, BREAKING CHANGE) still
#   need their own blank line above them.
